WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
Colorado Springs.

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.869
Families affected by the deadly shooting

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.938
at an LGBTQ club

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.473
gathered for Thanksgiving dinner

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.440
where they could mourn

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.709
the five people lost together.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.211
There has also been a remarkable

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.013
show of support for one of the heroes

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.114
in that attack.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.016
Richard Fiero took down the shooter

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.450
and with the help of two others,

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.418
beat the gunman.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.619
Stopping the rampage

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.821
hero and his wife own a local brewery.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.390
And in a Thanksgiving Day message,

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.357
they thanked supporters

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.959
who showed up to their business

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.093
and said they've been flooded

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.996
with company T-shirt orders

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.768
He are overwhelmed

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.137
by the love and support

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.238
everyone is giving us.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.873
And we feel it.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.075
All the comments,

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.978
just an outpouring of love

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:45.912
and it's beautiful

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.415
and we just want to thank everyone.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.050
We are very, very, very,

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.619
very grateful for every one of you.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.553
As part of your party,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.621
that will be the family home.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.922
Our intent is to keep

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.590
to field everybody's

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.125
request and get everybody assured.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.226
It may take us a year.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.195
It may take us ten days. Who knows?

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.865
And Richard joins me now.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.901
Richard, I'll take one of those T-shirts

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.903
to my hats off to you

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.439
for for your heroism.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.474
Tonight marks one week

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.444
since this horrific attack happened.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.179
Tell us how you're doing

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.115
We just got done

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.249
with a celebration of life.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.318
And, you know,

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:28.321
this isn't this is a life changing event

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:29.856
where everybody

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:30.857
in their building and

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.860
and their families and their friends.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.395
Yesterday, we were able to

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.229
open our brewery

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.664
and the girls that worked

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.265
there wanted to do so

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.434
for more or more for community to gather.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.970
And it was a beautiful, beautiful day.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:45.839
I couldn't think enough people.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:46.840
I tried to thank everyone

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.341
that walked through the door.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.743
But it was it was something that that I'm

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.278
very thankful

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.280
that that everybody's showing love.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.849
And hopefully we can we can

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.883
we can do a lot more of that.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.353
And the president called you.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.454
Tell us about that call.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.957
What what did he have to say?

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:07.427
And I guess what has that been like?

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.329
Well, I listen, I'm just I'm

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.865
just a young kid. I grew up in San Diego.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.533
I never expected to ever talk

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.167
to a president,

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.168
more or less

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.937
be around with any of that stuff,

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.839
a governor, a mayor.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.742
I am humbled,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.677
you know, at the end of the day.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.945
I wish everybody could talk to him

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.914
just just to have that honor

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.215
I'm a I'm an old soldier.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:29.616
For me

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.984
just to talk to the commander in chief

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.785
is is a big deal.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.554
So, you know,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:35.755
the discussion was between us

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.290
and I and I was very grateful

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.659
that he took the time to say

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.160
thank you

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.162
and and just kind of

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:44.063
send his condolences about the families.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.766
And Richard, you had a week to reflect

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:47.467
on what's happened.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.135
And I know you must be going through

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.737
so many different emotions.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.372
I'm just curious,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.507
what changes would you like to see?

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.643
We know the president has been saying

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.677
in the last couple of days

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:00.246
that he would like to see the country

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.447
take another

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.316
try at an assault weapons

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.617
ban in this country.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.285
I mean, obviously,

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:06.753
that's going to be difficult to get past.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.488
But do you have any thoughts on

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.489
what you would like to see,

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.224
what needs to happen in this country

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.492
so we don't have any more of these

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.227
mass shootings?

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.763
Well, Jim, I'll be honest.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.064
I was trained on a weapon

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.465
as a as a soldier.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.800
I respect weapons.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.970
My wife's got a concealed carry license.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:24.804
License.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:25.505
I mean, we

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.973
we we own guns

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.975
and we don't own guns, but we we

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.810
we work with guns.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.146
So, again, it's something for the nation

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.547
to figure out in the end

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.082
and whether that's administration

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.450
doesn't matter to me.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.418
I would just like people

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.653
to stop having so much anger.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:41.454
You know, it

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.356
shouldn't be something that's tense.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.657
There's no reason for somebody

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.593
to to go to a dance club

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.394
or a show or anything

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.463
and have to worry about being shot.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.331
I don't know

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.632
if that has anything to do with guns.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.666
I just think people need to be

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.667
a little bit nicer to each other.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.270
Absolutely.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.838
And your family's brewery just reopened

00:03:58.838 --> 00:03:59.639
for the first time

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.273
since the mass

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:00.640
shooting

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.875
and people were lined up outside.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.712
Tell us about this reception

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:08.014
and this outpouring of love

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.083
that your business has received

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.517
since the shooting.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.621
Yeah, it was it was it was humbling.

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:16.022
I I literally

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.390
we did not plan on being there.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.292
We didn't want to make this a thing.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.628
And, you know, it was just so much

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.263
we had to go back and help the girls

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.597
with with everything

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.065
they Everybody wiped us out.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.333
It was it was beautiful.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.735
As a business person.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.769
And it was more beautiful

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.336
as a person

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.070
to see

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:31.971
the variance,

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:32.705
that difference,

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.573
the adversity,

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.942
exclusion of everyone there.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.076
Everybody in the same room

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:40.113
just having some joy and enjoying a beer.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:41.114
You know,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.248
I tried to shake everyone's hand

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.817
and think of all I'm not a hero.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.252
You know, everybody else in that room

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.654
was a hero with us.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.589
Everybody's got a hero story

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.190
to just try and survive.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.126
And we lost five.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.327
And there's still many more in the house.

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:54.594
One more.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.862
My wife just went down to go

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.430
see our friends, Chip and Joanne.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.998
And, you know,

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.366
they got a long road to go.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.101
And when all these cameras are gone,

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:02.568
we're still going to

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:03.269
be live in this thing.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.307
And I mean, that that is the issue is,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:07.774
isn't it,

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:08.841
Richard is

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.542
in that

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.376
we're probably going

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.778
to have another one of these.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:13.112
We have had one

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.048
since what happened in Colorado Springs.

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.149
We had the mass shooting

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:18.251
at the Wal-Mart and Virginia.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:19.352
I guess

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.420
what are your thoughts on that,

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.621
that this keeps happening

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:24.991
in this country over and over again?

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:25.925
Again, like I said,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.261
I think just people need to start

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.462
loving each other, man.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.898
I hug and shake hands with folks

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.032
yesterday

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.268
that I'd never seen or met in my life.

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.569
I think folks need to do a little bit

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.337
more of that.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.138
And, you know,

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.274
there's this whole anger thing.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:41.941
And in people

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.843
picking teams, it's not cool.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.812
We all need to shake hands

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.680
and move forward, move to the action.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.749
And that action needs to be more caring

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:52.251
and more love across across this nation.

